    {
        "content": "<p>Something I've thought would be cool is if <code>use y := 42</code> could work</p>",
        "id": 585321295,
        "sender_full_name": "Kyle Miller",
        "timestamp": 1776135013
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"306601\">Kyle Miller</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Nested.20existential.20and.20.60use.60/near/585321295\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Something I've thought would be cool is if <code>use y := 42</code> could work</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>that would be extremely nice, indeed!</p>",
        "id": 585420184,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776171854
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This also works, but perhaps not what you were looking for:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bla</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- can this be transformed into the goal</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- ∃(x : α), (42 &gt; 1) ∧ x = x</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">conv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">enter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"n\">exists_and_right</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">exists_comm</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">use</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">42</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 585506993,
        "sender_full_name": "Dan Velleman",
        "timestamp": 1776194636
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah that's a lot of work for something seemingly simple</p>",
        "id": 585619869,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776247619
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"306601\">Kyle Miller</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Nested.20existential.20and.20.60use.60/near/585321295\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Something I've thought would be cool is if <code>use y := 42</code> could work</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I have given this some thought, and one problem with this is, that bound variables names are currently pretty unstable e.g. with simp</p>",
        "id": 585620089,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776247686
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe a conv version of <code>use</code> would be the best one can do until bound variables are being tracked through simp etc</p>",
        "id": 585620790,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1776247915
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that you can't just apply <code>use</code> to any existential quantifier anywhere in the goal.  For example, suppose the goal is <code>∃ (x : α), (∃y, y &gt; 1) → x ≠ x</code>.  This is false, so you shouldn't be able to prove it.  But if you were allowed to do <code>use y := 0</code>, then the goal would become <code>∃ (x : α), 0 &gt; 1 → x ≠ x</code>, which you could then prove (as long as there's something of type <code>α</code>).  So some justification is needed if you want to apply <code>use</code> to an existential quantifier inside the goal.  In <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"933054\">@Snir Broshi</span> 's solution, the justification involved giving a proof of <code>∀ (x : α), 42 &gt; 1 ∧ x = x → (∃ y, y &gt; 1) ∧ x = x</code> and then using <code>Exists.imp</code>.  In my solution, it involved using <code>exists_and_right</code> and <code>exists_comm</code>.</p>\n<p>Do we have a tactic that puts a proposition in prenex form?  That might be useful here.</p>",
        "id": 585687651,
        "sender_full_name": "Dan Velleman",
        "timestamp": 1776265750
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That's a \"negative occurrence\" of an existential though, and which is equivalent to a universal quantifier, so I wouldn't expect to be able to be able to do <code>use y := 0</code> there.</p>\n<p>The specification I'm imagining for <code>use</code> is \"interpret the goal as a tree of existentials, conjunctions, and leaf propositions, then use the provided values and proofs to eliminate a subset of these\". A leaf proposition might contain existentials, but these are outside the purview of <code>use</code>. Also, I'm taking \"existential\" loosely, and really I mean \"types with a single constructor\".</p>\n<p>Rather than <code>use y := 0</code>, something that could work more reliably is <code>use -, 0</code>, where <code>-</code> means \"I do not want to give a value right now\". The idea would then be that, rather than <code>use ?_, 0</code>, would would give a separate goal for the witness, <code>use -, 0</code> would use existentials to reassemble a single goal.</p>",
        "id": 585700316,
        "sender_full_name": "Kyle Miller",
        "timestamp": 1776268768
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There would be cases where <code>use y := 0</code> could be useful. For example, if the goal is an inductive proposition <code>I</code> and its constructor <code>I.c</code> has a field named <code>y</code>, then <code>use y := 0</code> could be a way to set just that field value, then reduce the goal to some existentials and conjunctions.</p>",
        "id": 585700661,
        "sender_full_name": "Kyle Miller",
        "timestamp": 1776268846
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"306601\">Kyle Miller</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Nested.20existential.20and.20.60use.60/near/585700316\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That's a \"negative occurrence\" of an existential though, and which is equivalent to a universal quantifier, so I wouldn't expect to be able to be able to do <code>use y := 0</code> there.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Right.  I wasn't sure if everyone reading this thread was aware of that issue, so I thought it was worthwhile to bring it up.</p>\n<p>Your proposal for a generalized <code>use</code> sounds interesting.</p>",
        "id": 585701970,
        "sender_full_name": "Dan Velleman",
        "timestamp": 1776269158
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Nested.20existential.20and.20.60use.60/near/585287072\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Tried that before, didn't work</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- error: Tactic `grewrite` failed: b is not a relation -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">substring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>You can use <code>apply_rw</code> (which is just a version of <code>grw</code> that doesn't strip the hypothesis <code>a</code> from <code>h</code>):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
